  "text": "Greenhouse gases are gases in Earth's atmosphere that trap heat. They let sunlight pass through the atmosphere, but they prevent the heat that the sunlight brings from leaving the atmosphere. The more greenhouse gases there are, the more heat energy is trapped in the atmosphere. This process is known as the greenhouse effect, and it is a major driver of climate change.\n\nThe fastest land animal in the world is the cheetah."
